.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH dotman 1  "dotman 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
dotman \- A dotfiles manager with no learning curve, safe by default
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdotman\fR [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
A dotfiles manager with no learning curve, safe by default
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress informational messages
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Disable pager output
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR
Allow running as root
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
dotman\-init(1)
Create the dotman repo or set its remote, or clone a repo and apply it
.TP
dotman\-add(1)
Start managing files or directories
.TP
dotman\-forget(1)
Stop managing files or directories, keeping them in $HOME
.TP
dotman\-list(1)
List the managed files
.TP
dotman\-status(1)
Compare $HOME, the repo and the last applied state
.TP
dotman\-apply(1)
Write the repo\*(Aqs files into $HOME
.TP
dotman\-diff(1)
Show how $HOME differs from the repo, as a diff from repo/ to home/
.TP
dotman\-edit(1)
Open a managed file\*(Aqs source in $VISUAL or $EDITOR, then apply it
.TP
dotman\-sync(1)
Capture local changes, commit, pull, apply what arrived and push
.TP
dotman\-log(1)
Show the repo\*(Aqs history
.TP
dotman\-restore(1)
Write an earlier version of a file into $HOME, keeping the current one as a backup
.TP
dotman\-import(1)
Convert another setup into the repo, or add what the repo lacks from one
.TP
dotman\-git(1)
Run git in the repo
.TP
dotman\-doctor(1)
Check the environment and the repo for problems
.TP
dotman\-key(1)
Create or import the age identity that decrypts encrypted files
.TP
dotman\-completion(1)
Generate shell completion scripts
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success. \fBstatus\fR exits 0 even when it lists paths to look at.
.TP
\fB1\fR
An error. \fBdoctor\fR also exits 1 when one of its checks fails.
.TP
\fB2\fR
The command line could not be parsed.
.TP
\fB3\fR
The run finished, but left paths for you: undecided, held back,
blocked, or reported for action.
.TP
\fB4\fR
\fBsync\fR hit a rebase conflict, aborted the pull and printed the
steps to resolve it; or a git operation or conflict is unfinished
in the repo.
.PP
The \fBgit\fR subcommand exits with git\*(Aqs own status.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBDOTMAN_REPO_PATH\fR
The repo, as an absolute path. It wins over \fBrepo\fR in the machine
config. Default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/dotman.
.TP
\fBDOTMAN_CONFIG_PATH\fR
The machine config, as an absolute path.
Default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dotman/config.toml.
.TP
\fBDOTMAN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR
Any non\-empty value asks nothing, as when stdin is not a terminal.
Paths a prompt would decide are skipped and listed, and the run
exits 3.
.TP
\fBDOTMAN_ALLOW_ROOT\fR
1 lets dotman run as root, as \-\-allow\-root does.
.TP
\fBDOTMAN_AGE_KEY\fR
The text of an age identity. It reaches age only on its stdin, and
every other child process starts without it.
.TP
\fBDOTMAN_AGE_KEY_FILE\fR
An age identity file, as an absolute path, tried before the
identity file in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dotman.
.TP
\fBDOTMAN_HOST\fR
Replaces the host name, detected or set under [identity] in the
machine config, for variants and templates.
.TP
\fBDOTMAN_PROFILES\fR
Comma\-separated profiles that replace the machine config\*(Aqs.
.TP
\fBDOTMAN_APPROVE_HOOKS, DOTMAN_BOOTSTRAP_BASE_URL\fR
Read by the install.sh that \fBinit\fR writes, not by dotman: 1
approves the repo\*(Aqs hooks, and the URL replaces the release
download base.
.TP
\fBDOTMAN_SYSTEM_ROOT, DOTMAN_NIX_STORE\fR
For tests only; \fBdoctor\fR warns when either is set. The system\-write
helper refuses DOTMAN_SYSTEM_ROOT when it runs as root.
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
Turns colour off.
.TP
\fBNO_PAGER\fR
Any non\-empty value makes \fBdiff\fR skip the pager, as \-\-no\-pager does.
.TP
\fBVISUAL, EDITOR\fR
The editor \fBedit\fR starts; VISUAL wins.
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME\fR
Where the machine config, the repo and the state with its backups
live. Each defaults under $HOME.
.TP
\fBXDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR
Where \fBdiff\fR puts its private temporary copies; the state
directory when it is unset.
.TP
\fBRUST_LOG\fR
A tracing filter for debug output on stderr. Default: warn.
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
